  "question": {
    "text": "In a photoelectric experiment, with light of wavelength $\\lambda,$ the fastest electron has speed $v$. If the exciting wavelength is changed to $3 \\lambda / 4$, the speed of the fastest emitted electron will become",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HeLmX",
      "text": "$v \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "NrrvK",
      "text": "$v \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9I7lp",
      "text": "less than $v \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ho6jU",
      "text": "greater than $v \\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{mv}^{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{\\lambda}-\\phi$\n$$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\frac{1}{2} \\mathrm{~m}^{\\prime}=\\frac{\\mathrm{hc}}{(3 \\lambda / 4)}-\\phi=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{hc}}{3 \\lambda}-\\phi \\\\\n\\text { Clearly, } \\mathrm{v}^{\\prime}>\\sqrt{\\frac{4}{3} \\mathrm{v}}\n\\end{array}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
